From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: pin NtSetIoCompletion to 0xe9

WoW Classic's loader enters the pop-rsp probe when the
NtSetIoCompletion export's mov eax immediate is the Windows 10
build 19045 id 0x1a3. Forever's hole-fill, and the pre-1246
console, leave that immediate at 0xe9. Those calls returned.
NtFlushInstructionCache takes the next free id, 0x1da, and 0x1a3
stays empty. The 32-bit list is unchanged. No console run.
---
diff --git a/tools/make_specfiles b/tools/make_specfiles
--- a/tools/make_specfiles
+++ b/tools/make_specfiles
@@ -451,6 +451,32 @@
         $used{$id} = $name;
         $syscall->[2] = $id;
     }
+
+    # WoW Classic reads the mov eax immediate of the NtSetIoCompletion export.
+    # 0x1a3 is the Windows 10 19045 number, and that immediate is what sends
+    # the loader into the pop-rsp probe (ntdll+0x58340 in the 19045 image,
+    # wine-child 151). Forever's hole-fill, with this assignment not applied,
+    # leaves that export at 0xe9. The pre-1246 console log used 0xe9 and the
+    # calls returned without that probe. Pin the export back to 0xe9.
+    # NtFlushInstructionCache holds 0xe9 in the Windows table, so it takes the
+    # next free id. 0x1a3 stays empty: no stub carries the Windows immediate.
+    my ($completion, $flush);
+    foreach my $syscall (@$syscalls)
+    {
+        $completion = $syscall if $syscall->[0] eq 'NtSetIoCompletion';
+        $flush = $syscall if $syscall->[0] eq 'NtFlushInstructionCache';
+    }
+    die "NtSetIoCompletion missing from the 64-bit list\n" unless $completion;
+    die "NtFlushInstructionCache missing from the 64-bit list\n" unless $flush;
+    die "19045 NtSetIoCompletion id changed\n" if $completion->[2] != 0x1a3;
+    die "19045 NtFlushInstructionCache id changed\n" if $flush->[2] != 0xe9;
+    die "no free id for NtFlushInstructionCache\n" if $next >= 0x1000 || $used{$next};
+    delete $used{$flush->[2]};
+    $flush->[2] = $next;
+    $used{$next} = $flush->[0];
+    delete $used{$completion->[2]};
+    $completion->[2] = 0xe9;
+    $used{0xe9} = $completion->[0];
 }
 
 sub update_syscalls($$$$;$)
